i3status-rust (0.36.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release
  * Build-Depend on cmake, git and libclang-dev. The speedtest block now
    uses cf-mach, whose boring-sys builds a vendored BoringSSL with cmake,
    generates its bindings with bindgen, and runs git unconditionally to
    apply a patch. The builder image ships git, so only a rebuilder would
    have missed it.
  * Drop libssl-dev: reqwest moved to rustls and nothing links OpenSSL.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:28:59 +0200

i3status-rust (0.36.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stamp the upstream commit from debian/upstream-commit. build.rs shells
    out to git, the builder removes the clone's .git, and Command::output()
    returns Ok on a failed git -- so upstream's fallback never fired and
    0.36.1-1 shipped "0.36.1 (commit  )".

